From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:49:07 +0900
Subject: Compile a unit read from TASTy with the language settings it was
 compiled with

A unit compiled with capture checking, or with pure functions, enabled by a
command-line option rather than by a language import, carries no trace of it
in its trees, and a run which recompiled it from TASTy went by the options it
was given itself. The phases after capture checking go by the setting
(`UncacheGivenAliases`, the pattern matcher, the inliner), so without the
option repeated the unit was compiled to other code than from source: a given
alias that was cached became a plain method. A run over a classpath mixing
units compiled with and without the option could not be given one set of
options that suited both.

The unit's TASTy attributes record both settings. `ReadTasty` now restores
them on the unit, and marks capture checking as enabled somewhere in the run,
as the option would. `UncacheGivenAliases` keeps a given alias cached when
capture checking is on anywhere in a run from source, since a checked unit can
name the alias of another; a run from TASTy checks no captures, so there it
goes by the unit itself, and each unit of a mixed run gets the code it had.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: tastyattrs
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/fromtasty/ReadTasty.scala   | 8 ++++++++
 .../dotty/tools/dotc/transform/UncacheGivenAliases.scala  | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/fromtasty/ReadTasty.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/fromtasty/ReadTasty.scala
index eccc5144b710e36684009310a1331b0f7338cae3..8d75fc3ab04d3be9f8d7256d11956026705c15c2 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/fromtasty/ReadTasty.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/fromtasty/ReadTasty.scala
@@ -56,6 +56,14 @@ class ReadTasty extends Phase {
                 else
                   val unit = CompilationUnit(cls, cls.rootTree, forceTrees = true)
                   unit.pickled += (cls -> (() => unpickler.unpickler.bytes))
+                  // A unit compiled with capture checking or pure functions, enabled by an
+                  // option rather than by an import in its tree, says so only in its
+                  // attributes. The phases after them go by these settings, so without them
+                  // the unit would be compiled to other code than it was from source.
+                  if attributes.captureChecked then
+                    unit.needsCaptureChecking = true
+                    ctx.run.nn.ccEnabledSomewhere = true
+                  if attributes.withPureFuns then unit.knowsPureFuns = true
                   Some(unit)
               }
             case tree: Tree[?] =>
diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/UncacheGivenAliases.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/UncacheGivenAliases.scala
index 5980887a3828529ab526705c1a9b6cd0a398d04a..cf9aae5a84dc919f17e16ca3041fb1f29704a7a7 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/UncacheGivenAliases.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/UncacheGivenAliases.scala
@@ -59,8 +59,10 @@ class UncacheGivenAliases extends MiniPhase with IdentityDenotTransformer:
     // to a def gives it an ExprType underlying, which is no longer a legal capability
     // and crashes cc Setup (IllegalCaptureRef) when a later cast or summon forces the
     // set. Skip the optimization when cc is on anywhere; semantics are unchanged.
+    // A run from TASTy checks no captures, and only has to give each unit the code
+    // it was compiled to, so it goes by whether the unit itself was capture-checked.
     if sym.isAllOf(LazyGiven) && !needsCache(sym, tree.rhs)
-        && !Feature.ccEnabledSomewhere then
+        && !(if ctx.settings.fromTasty.value then Feature.ccEnabled else Feature.ccEnabledSomewhere) then
       sym.copySymDenotation(
         initFlags = sym.flags &~ Lazy | Method,
         info = ExprType(sym.info))
